# ${SRC_DIR}/api/${API_VERSION}/

API version ${API_VERSION} for ${PROJECT_NAME}.

## What lives here

- One folder per feature, named after the feature (lowercase, plural).
- The `_feature_template/` exemplar — copy it and rename to start a new feature.
- The working `health/` feature — a real `GET /healthz` example.

## The strict 4-subfolder rule

Every feature folder under this version has exactly:

- `routes/` — `*.routes.ts` (route registration)
- `controllers/` — `*.controller.ts` (request handlers)
- `services/` — `*.service.ts` (business logic)
- `types/` — `*.types.ts` (request/response and domain types)

No file lives at a feature root — the feature's `README.md` is the only
top-level item inside a feature folder.

## Adding a feature

1. Copy `_feature_template/` to `<your-feature>/`.
2. Rename the `__FEATURE__.*` placeholders.
3. Fill in the four subfolders.
4. Mount the router in `${SRC_DIR}/app.ts`.

